                <pb facs="0270" n="174" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg174"/>

                <head>No. 90.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Osborn to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States.</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago, Chili</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-04-26"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 26, 1879</date>.
                        (Received June 3.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 96.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: For your information I have the honor to
                    inclose a copy of a note which I have this day written to Mr. Christiancy, at
                    Lima, concerning the status of foreign-built vessels owned by American
                    citizens.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>THOMAS A. OSBORN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
